{"title":"An experiment for our schools","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/964481804/0/marginalrevolution~An-experiment-for-our-schools.html","date":1785398875000,"content":"<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p>Schools in at least three states will be equipped with drones this year that can zoom through halls, smash windows and pepper-spray active shooters if teachers report a threat.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<div>\r\n<p>At least nine schools — three in Florida, five in Georgia and one in Colorado — will have storage boxes that house the plastic, nonlethal aircraft made by Austin-based Mithril Defense. The drones, which can be activated by teachers, are capable of reaching a shooter within 15 seconds.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p>The aircraft are designed to distract their targets by flashing strobes, blaring sirens, spraying them with pepper gel, or ramming into them at 60 mph.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2026/07/28/schools-are-adding-pepper-spraying-drones-help-combat-active-shooters/\" target=\"_blank\">the full piece</a>.  As I have been saying, be long countries where local crime is a major problem.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/an-experiment-for-our-schools.html\">An experiment for our schools</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/964481804/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/964481804/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/964481804/margi